WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.590
Two devices, two mini cables, total guessing.

2
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:11.590
Meet ClariWatt Duo, a dual USB-C charging cable with a built-in power display.

3
00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:15.590
Connect it to a compatible USB-C PC source.

4
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:21.590
Then charge two devices through one split cable with up to 140 watts shared.

5
00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.590
The screen shows total input and C1 and C2 branch readings.

6
00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:30.590
So when a second device joins, you can see how power is shared.

7
00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:36.590
Use it with a laptop and phone at your desk, or with everyday USB-C gear while traveling.

8
00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:40.590
It also works with compatible USB-C DVD power banks.

9
00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:47.590
One branch supports USB-2 data, up to 480 megabits per second, while the other charges.

10
00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:52.590
That's ClariWatt Duo on Kickstarter, clarity in every watt.
